            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A computer-implemented method of generating a share of a threshold signature, wherein a group of participants comprises a set of target participants and a set of dummy participants, wherein the number of target participants is less than the number of participants required to generate a valid signature, wherein each target participant and each dummy participants has i) a respective share of a first private key, ii) a respective share of an ephemeral private key, iii) a respective share of a first blinding key, iv) a respective share of a second blinding key, and wherein each target participant has v) an ephemeral public key corresponding to the ephemeral private key.</p>
